### 3. AI-Powered Flashcard System (Must)

This is the biggest new feature. The user enters a topic → backend generates flashcards via the RAG/AI system → displayed as swipeable cards.

#### [NEW] [flashcardService.ts](file:///e:/KTUfy_Project/ktufy-frontend/KTUfy/services/flashcardService.ts)

New service to call backend, following existing [chatService.ts](file:///e:/KTUfy_Project/ktufy-frontend/KTUfy/services/chatService.ts) pattern:

```typescript
// POST /api/v1/flashcards/generate
// Request: { topic: string, count?: number }
// Response: { flashcards: [{ front: string, back: string }] }
export async function generateFlashcards(topic: string, count?: number)
```

#### [MODIFY] [ExploreScreen.tsx](file:///e:/KTUfy_Project/ktufy-frontend/KTUfy/screens/ExploreScreen.tsx)

Add a new tool card for Flashcards, or repurpose the existing Learning Zone flashcard section:

```diff
+{ key: 'Flashcards', label: 'AI Flashcards', icon: '🎴', desc: 'Generate flashcards by topic', color: '#8B5CF6' },
```

#### Two implementation approaches:

**Option A — Separate screen (recommended):** Create a dedicated `FlashcardScreen.tsx` with topic input + generated cards. Add to navigation.

**Option B — Integrate into Learning Zone:** Replace the static flashcards in [LearningZoneScreen.tsx](file:///e:/KTUfy_Project/ktufy-frontend/KTUfy/screens/LearningZoneScreen.tsx) with AI-generated ones via a topic input field.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Which approach do you prefer?** Separate screen (Option A) or part of Learning Zone (Option B)?
>
> Also, **does your backend already have a `/api/v1/flashcards/generate` endpoint**, or should I build the frontend assuming you'll add it later?

