### 5. Coding Hub — Code Execution API

#### [MODIFY] [CodingHubScreen.tsx](file:///e:/KTUfy_Project/ktufy-frontend/KTUfy/screens/CodingHubScreen.tsx)

Currently [runCode()](file:///e:/KTUfy_Project/ktufy-frontend/KTUfy/screens/CodingHubScreen.tsx#256-337) (line 256-336) uses **fake simulation** — it pattern-matches keywords like "hello" and "world" in the code string. This needs to be replaced with a real code execution API.

**Two options:**

| Option | Approach | Cost | Latency |
|--------|----------|------|---------|
| **A. Judge0 API** | Free hosted API, send code + language, get output | Free (50 req/day) or self-hosted | ~2-5s |
| **B. Your backend** | Add `POST /api/v1/coding/execute` endpoint with sandboxed execution | Free but needs setup | ~1-3s |

> [!WARNING]
> **Overhead assessment:** Adding code execution is moderate overhead. The frontend change is simple (~30 lines replacing the simulation). The complexity is on the backend side (sandboxing). Using Judge0's free API is the easiest path with minimal overhead.

**Recommendation:** Start with Judge0 free tier for MVP, migrate to your own backend later if needed.

